"A concrete version of this shows up in the liver-lung relationship. Metal (the lung) normally controls wood (the liver), the way a blade keeps a tree in check. But if the liver becomes excessively strong — from prolonged frustration, for instance — it can overwhelm the lung instead, a pattern sometimes described as \"wood insulting metal.\" A person in this pattern may show liver-type symptoms, like irritability, alongside lung-type symptoms, like coughing or shortness of breath, in a combination that looks backward compared to the expected controlling direction.": "7ecf6c27e682",
